            <ArticleTitle>[Translaminar fenestration for caudally herniated lumbar discs--a technical note].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>597-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1055/s-0029-1186107</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Translaminar approaches have been described for lumbar disc herniations which are displaced cranially or laterally into the neuroforamen. This technique provides the advantages of a minimally invasive approach with regard to postoperative instability or partial facet joint resection and avoids a medial arthrectomy. We describe this technique for the first time as an option for a caudally sequestrated disc herniation via a transaxillar sequesterotomy.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Georg Thieme Verlag KG Stuttgart, New York.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
